176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (Since our founding in 1999, the Partnership for Scientific Inquiry \(PSI\) has evolved significantly. We are launching this annual newsletter to celebrate our students' achievements and to stay connected with you, our PSI alumni community.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (PSI remains a distinctive and unique opportunity for high school students to engage deeply with the scientific community. Our "prep then practice" philosophy combines a semester-long lecture series and one-on-one mentorship with a hands-on internship. We focus on training students to think like scientists while teaching practical, hands-on skills that build confidence in the lab. This integrated approach makes this experience so impactful for our participants.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 168 0 R
/E (In recent years, we have intentionally strengthened our focus on supporting students who are traditionally underrepresented in STEM or face significant barriers to accessing scientific careers. Our goal is to cultivate the next generation of scientists, clinicians, and educators, ensuring that PSI serves as a meaningful stepping stone in their professional journeys.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
