396 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 173 0 R
/E (When I was growing up, I rarely saw anyone like me in science or medicine. My parents did not attend college and lacked access to the networks that often serve as gateways into this field. Through PSI, I connected with BIPOC students and I saw myself represented in the scientific community for the first time. PSI showed me that I was part of a community that truly belonged in science. The most meaningful moment of this program was presenting my research at the PSI symposium. Standing in a room with my family, mentors, and peers, I felt a sense of belonging and empowerment unlike anything I had experienced before. This program gave me access to so many amazing experiences and opportunities, and I )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
